        is literally true (bounded by the Space's bases and connections). For Schema changes,
        Documentation updates, and these two once a Space passes 25 bases, it is not: the set is
        bounded by the reporting WINDOW. Since the contract now warns in production instead of
        throwing, the failure mode is a console line and a long table rather than a 500 — which is
        the right degradation, and still not the same thing as a correct answer. What the vessel is
        missing is a third value for "a document snapshot renders every row, unpaged, on purpose".
