    >
        {/* NARROW CLASSIFICATION — the base leads. This table is FOR "how much record data is in
            each base", so Records is the one number and the storage figure — the section's actual
            subject — is the second line, with the table count beside it. Fields goes off: it is the
            finest-grained structural count, it is stated per base in Schema Browse and in this
            report's own Backup summary columns, and one of the two sub slots has to hold size. */}
        {dataHealth.records.byBase.map((b) => (
